### SOCGPT API samples (VS Code "REST Client" extension). Run "Sign in" first.

# @name login
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "manager1", "password": "Manager@123" }

### Who am I
GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Send a raw event as a sensor (no sign-in, uses the ingest key)
POST http://localhost:8080/events
Content-Type: application/json
X-Ingest-Key: dev-ingest-key

{ "sourceIp": "10.0.0.99", "eventType": "sqli", "mitreId": "T1190" }

### Incidents list
GET http://localhost:8080/api/incidents
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### One incident (report, plan, risk factors, chain, similar incidents, permissions)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/1
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Attack chains
GET http://localhost:8080/api/chains
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Dashboard numbers
GET http://localhost:8080/api/stats
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Approve a plan (analysts: non-critical only; critical needs a SOC manager)
POST http://localhost:8080/remediation-plans/1/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Reject a plan with a reason
POST http://localhost:8080/remediation-plans/2/reject?reason=Too%20disruptive
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Run the simulated recovery (SOC manager or admin, only after approval)
POST http://localhost:8080/remediation-plans/1/execute
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Re-run the AI on an OPEN incident
POST http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/2/reinvestigate
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Launch a simulated attack (optionally from a fixed IP)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/simulate?type=port_scan&ip=203.0.113.50
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### PDF report
GET http://localhost:8080/api/incidents/1/report.pdf
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Create a user (admin only)
POST http://localhost:8080/users
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "analyst2", "email": "analyst2@socgpt.com", "password": "Analyst@456", "role": "analyst" }

### Re-index the AI's memory of past incidents (admin only)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/rag/reindex
Authorization: Bearer {{login.response.body.token}}

### Talk to the Python agent directly
POST http://localhost:8000/investigate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "incidentId": 99, "severity": "CRITICAL", "riskScore": 90,
  "eventType": "sqli", "sourceIp": "10.0.0.99", "mitreId": "T1190",
  "techniqueName": "Exploit Public-Facing Application", "tactic": "Initial Access",
  "csfFunction": "Protect", "csfDescription": "Safeguards limit the impact."
}

### Embedding endpoint
POST http://localhost:8000/embed
Content-Type: application/json

{ "text": "Attack: sqli. Tactic: Initial Access.", "kind": "query" }
